---
description: JRebirth boundaries and forbidden shortcuts
alwaysApply: true
---
# JRebirth boundaries

Always prefer mechanisms the framework already provides over ad-hoc shortcuts.

The following shortcuts are banned by default:

- no `new Thread` in normal application flow
- no `Platform.runLater` used as a design pattern
- no heavy business logic placed inside View or Controller
- no stateful bindings owned by the View when they belong in the Model
- no `localFacade().globalFacade()` except rare hard integration cases

Whenever in doubt, stop and use the relevant skill under `jrebirth-ai-kit/skills/` (for example `jrebirth-threading`, `jrebirth-anti-patterns`).
